1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,630
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,630 --> 00:00:05,070
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:06,230
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,810
I've set tile most of my
life.

5
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:11,570
Bathrooms, kitchens,
shower pans,

6
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:12,720
tub surrounds.

7
00:00:12,790 --> 00:00:14,290
Most of it on my knees,

8
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:15,750
on hard floors.

9
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:16,810
I had my right knee

10
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:18,240
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:20,060
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,470
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:22,690
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:23,610
and it went away.

15
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:24,770
This is different.

16
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:25,180
Tight.

17
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:25,800
Full.

18
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:26,770
Like a band around

19
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:28,360
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,640
And for two years I've

21
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,070
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:32,340
Give it time.

23
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:34,340
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:35,660
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:36,940
At three months,

26
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:37,990
give it six.

27
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:38,830
At six months,

28
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:40,310
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:41,060
At a year,

30
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:42,990
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:44,600
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:46,230
We went down the list.

33
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,980
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:49,210
Every session,

35
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:50,750
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:51,940
I got stronger.

37
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,720
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:55,240
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,540
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,800
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:58,800 --> 00:00:59,910
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:01,140
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,850
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:04,990
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:06,340
And after that, a second

46
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:07,530
operation to go back

47
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:08,700
in and do it over.

48
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:09,820
I said no.

49
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,910
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

50
00:01:11,910 --> 00:01:12,920
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,590
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:16,960
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,500
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,290
for it and loaded the
truck anyway.

55
00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:21,350
On a job I'd get

56
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:22,480
down on the shower floor

57
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,790
to set the pan,

58
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:24,990
and it took two tries

59
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:25,980
and a hand on the tub

60
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:26,910
to get back up.

61
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:28,740
Down on the floor and up
again

62
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,270
a few hundred times a day,

63
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:31,280
and every one of them

64
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:32,340
cost me something.

65
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:35,060
At home I couldn't do the
stairs,

66
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:36,310
couldn't stand at the
counter

67
00:01:36,310 --> 00:01:38,060
long enough to finish
dinner,

68
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:39,790
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

69
00:01:39,790 --> 00:01:41,670
without shifting every two
minutes.

70
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,200
It woke me at night,

71
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,520
and it turned ordinary
things,

72
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,810
like getting in the truck

73
00:01:46,810 --> 00:01:48,210
or up off the couch,

74
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:49,340
into a decision.

75
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:50,670
And the thing I never

76
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:51,830
said out loud

77
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:53,120
was that I didn't know how
many

78
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,970
more bathrooms I had in
me.

79
00:01:55,290 --> 00:01:56,880
Tile is all I know

80
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:57,800
how to do.

81
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:59,150
After a long and serious

82
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:00,500
talk with my wife,

83
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,180
I went back in one more
time.

84
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:03,860
That was the fourth set

85
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,310
of X-rays on this knee.

86
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:07,210
And like the three before
it,

87
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:09,500
the answer was everything
looks great.

88
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:11,930
No loosening, no
infection,

89
00:02:11,930 --> 00:02:12,940
nothing wrong.

90
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:14,320
Only this time there

91
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:15,450
was no new number.

92
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,090
Nobody said give it
another six months.

93
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,090
There was nothing left to
give it.

94
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,600
I sat in the truck

95
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,270
in the parking lot for a
while.

96
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:24,130
Okay, I thought.

97
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:25,530
Then explain this.

98
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,870
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

99
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:29,340
I hit my breaking point.

100
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:31,720
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

101
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,830
Everyone in the house was
asleep

102
00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:35,700
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

103
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,820
with my leg up,

104
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,470
trying to find any angle
where

105
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:40,290
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

106
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,860
around my knee and
tightening.

107
00:02:42,190 --> 00:02:44,750
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

108
00:02:44,970 --> 00:02:46,780
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

109
00:02:47,090 --> 00:02:48,320
I had a shower floor

110
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,910
to set that Monday,

111
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:50,870
and I didn't know how I

112
00:02:50,870 --> 00:02:52,200
was going to get down
there.

113
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,630
And I just thought,

114
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:55,370
is this really my life
now?

115
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,950
I can't live like this.

116
00:02:56,990 --> 00:02:58,740
So I made myself a
promise.

117
00:02:58,890 --> 00:02:59,650
I wouldn't go a day

118
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:01,220
without looking for an
answer.

119
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,820
And when I found one,

120
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:04,050
I'd share it with everyone

121
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:05,520
going through the same
thing.

122
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,140
So I got my laptop

123
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,370
out and went looking.

124
00:03:08,610 --> 00:03:09,880
Not for a product.

125
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,190
For an explanation.

126
00:03:11,490 --> 00:03:13,100
Mayo Clinic forums,

127
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,560
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

128
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,840
a group for tile guys

129
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,060
with bad knees,

130
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:20,570
doctor videos, medical
animations.

131
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,320
And that's when I found a
video

132
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,160
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

133
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,750
Steven Salinger,

134
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:27,100
whose own wife had been

135
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,720
through exactly this.

136
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:30,210
But before I say anything
else,

137
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:31,510
I want to be straight with
you.

138
00:03:31,850 --> 00:03:33,820
You've already had
something work fast.

139
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:34,580
The ice.

140
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:36,390
The first week of a new
pill.

141
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:38,470
The good day after a
session.

142
00:03:38,610 --> 00:03:39,940
Then it wore off.

143
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:42,350
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

144
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:44,430
Fast relief isn't relief.

145
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:45,520
It's a preview.

146
00:03:45,690 --> 00:03:46,650
So I'm not going to tell

147
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:48,010
you this works fast.

148
00:03:48,050 --> 00:03:48,910
It doesn't.

149
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,090
But if you're willing to
be patient,

150
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:52,270
and to look at what's
going

151
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:53,900
on around your new knee

152
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,460
instead of inside it,

153
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:56,930
there is a real reason

154
00:03:56,930 --> 00:03:58,050
it still hurts.

155
00:03:58,190 --> 00:03:59,830
And something you can do
about it.

156
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:01,680
Let me explain what he
said,

157
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,200
because this is what
changed

158
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,390
everything for me.

159
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:06,380
He started with the
basics.

160
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:08,460
A knee replacement takes
out the worn

161
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,680
joint surfaces and puts in
metal

162
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,710
and plastic.

163
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,780
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

164
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:15,460
you had before the
operation.

165
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,190
That part I already knew.

166
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,930
But then he explained
something

167
00:04:18,930 --> 00:04:20,490
nobody had ever told me.

168
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,430
He said,

169
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:22,870
think about a swollen foot

170
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:24,080
inside a shoe.

171
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,580
The shoe didn't shrink.

172
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,450
Your foot is taking up
more room,

173
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:30,020
so everything feels
cramped

174
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,610
and tight and squeezed.

175
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:33,210
Your new knee sits

176
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:34,740
in a limited space

177
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,960
with living tissue packed
all around it.

178
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:39,480
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

179
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,100
had to work through that
tissue.

180
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:43,700
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

181
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,360
At first that's normal.

182
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,260
But in some people that
swelling can

183
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:49,910
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

184
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:51,840
And swollen tissue takes
up more

185
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:53,670
room than calm tissue
does.

186
00:04:53,770 --> 00:04:55,110
So when you bend,

187
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:56,870
that tissue gets
compressed.

188
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,130
When you straighten,

189
00:04:58,130 --> 00:04:59,460
it gets pulled tight.

190
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:00,910
That's the band.

191
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:03,540
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

192
00:05:03,610 --> 00:05:04,740
And you start being

193
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:05,980
the one who says,

194
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:07,440
you take the floor.

195
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:08,880
I'll do the walls.

196
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,710
And that's exactly why so
much

197
00:05:10,710 --> 00:05:12,870
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

198
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:15,240
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

199
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,220
around the knee.

200
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:17,240
Worth doing,

201
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,180
and I'd done it.

202
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:19,930
It does nothing about
tissue

203
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:21,080
taking up room.

204
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:22,510
A nerve block quiets

205
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:24,240
the nerve carrying the
signal.

206
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:26,470
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

207
00:05:26,850 --> 00:05:28,390
But when that irritated
tissue

208
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:29,910
finally calms down,

209
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:31,320
it holds less fluid,

210
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:32,800
and it takes up less room.

211
00:05:32,990 --> 00:05:34,240
Less room taken up means

212
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,890
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

213
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,800
That's what takes the
pressure off.

214
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:39,860
After two years of this,

215
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:41,650
it finally made sense.

216
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,100
The problem was never the
new knee.

217
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:46,510
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

218
00:05:46,630 --> 00:05:48,460
He calls it the squeeze.

219
00:05:48,530 --> 00:05:51,070
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

220
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:53,460
I'd bought gel knee pads,

221
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,630
a kneeling board, knee
sleeves,

222
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:57,080
compression braces,

223
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,570
creams, half of Amazon
really,

224
00:05:59,570 --> 00:06:00,840
and all any of it gave

225
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:01,910
me was an hour.

226
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,360
The pads made the floor
softer.

227
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,050
They did nothing about the
knee.

228
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,150
I even looked at going

229
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:09,400
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

230
00:06:09,630 --> 00:06:11,930
But at $200 a session

231
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:14,056
with nothing covered by
insurance,

232
00:06:14,056 --> 00:06:15,280
that was a quick no.

233
00:06:15,610 --> 00:06:16,590
Then one night I went

234
00:06:16,590 --> 00:06:17,850
back to that knee
replacement

235
00:06:17,850 --> 00:06:19,180
group and actually read
it.

236
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,090
Thousands of people,

237
00:06:21,090 --> 00:06:22,630
years out from surgery,

238
00:06:22,630 --> 00:06:24,070
comparing notes on
stiffness

239
00:06:24,070 --> 00:06:26,070
and tightness nobody could
explain.

240
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,640
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

241
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,250
the same thing kept coming
up.

242
00:06:29,570 --> 00:06:31,100
This one device,

243
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,300
and people saying

244
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,210
it was the first thing

245
00:06:33,210 --> 00:06:34,390
that made a difference.

246
00:06:34,710 --> 00:06:36,800
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

247
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:37,890
alright, here it comes,

248
00:06:37,890 --> 00:06:39,330
he's selling me something,

249
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:41,160
let me shut that down
right now.

250
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,220
I'm only here because I
made myself

251
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:45,440
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

252
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,430
that if I ever found

253
00:06:46,430 --> 00:06:47,670
something that helped,

254
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:48,690
I'd say so.

255
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:50,470
It's called the KenRelief
Red

256
00:06:50,470 --> 00:06:51,800
Light Therapy Wrap.

257
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,960
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

258
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,860
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

259
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,860
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

260
00:06:58,170 --> 00:07:00,060
But I went to their
website anyway,

261
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:00,910
just to see what all

262
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:02,100
the fuss was about.

263
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:04,490
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

264
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:07,290
charge $200 a session for,

265
00:07:07,290 --> 00:07:10,320
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

266
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,530
in a wrap you plug

267
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:12,740
into the wall at home.

268
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:14,520
Two hundred and forty
lights.

269
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:16,880
Red at 660 nanometers

270
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:19,240
and near-infrared at 850,

271
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,250
run together for the
strongest effect.

272
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:22,660
Four strength levels.

273
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:24,330
A five to thirty minute
timer.

274
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,140
Then I saw the guarantee.

275
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,240
Ninety days.

276
00:07:27,450 --> 00:07:29,920
Results or your money
back,

277
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,250
no questions,

278
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,640
no store credit,

279
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:34,570
and you don't even send it
back.

280
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:37,150
I stand behind every floor
I set.

281
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,650
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

282
00:07:39,650 --> 00:07:41,180
days to change my mind.

